{"content":[{"c":["SERAIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Royal secretary of King David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.8.17","r":"2Sam.8.17","rawR":"2Sam.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.8.17","value":"2Sam.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 8:17"},"); alternately called Sheva in ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.20.25","r":"2Sam.20.25","rawR":"2Sam.20.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.20.25","value":"2Sam.20.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 20:25"},", Shisha in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.3","r":"1Kgs.4.3","rawR":"1Kgs.4.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.3","value":"1Kgs.4.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kings 4:3"},", and Shavsha in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.18.16","r":"1Chr.18.16","rawR":"1Chr.18.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.18.16","value":"1Chr.18.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 18:16"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Chief priest in Jerusalem at the time of its destruction by the Babylonians in 586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". He was taken by Nebuzaradan, the captain of the guard, to Nebuchadnezzar at Riblah, where he was put to death (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.18","r":"2Kgs.25.18","rawR":"2Kgs.25.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.18","value":"2Kgs.25.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.52.24","r":"Jer.52.24","rawR":"Jer.52.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.52.24","value":"Jer.52.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 52:24"},"). ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.14","r":"1Chr.6.14","rawR":"1Chr.6.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.14","value":"1Chr.6.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"First Chronicles 6:14"}," records Seraiah as the son of Azariah, the father of Jehozadak and a descendant of Levi through Aaron’s line."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite and one of the captains of the Judean forces who sought clemency from Nebuchadnezzar under Gedaliah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.23","r":"2Kgs.25.23","rawR":"2Kgs.25.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.23","value":"2Kgs.25.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.40.8","r":"Jer.40.8","rawR":"Jer.40.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.40.8","value":"Jer.40.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 40:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Judahite, the son of Kenaz, the brother of Othniel and Joab’s father (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.13-14","r":"1Chr.4.13-14","rawR":"1Chr.4.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.13-14","value":"1Chr.4.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:13-14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Simeonite, the son of Asiel and Joshibiah’s father (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.35","r":"1Chr.4.35","rawR":"1Chr.4.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.35","value":"1Chr.4.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. One of the men who returned with Zerubbabel to Judah following the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.2","r":"Ezra.2.2","rawR":"Ezra.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.2","value":"Ezra.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:2"},"); called Azariah in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.7","r":"Neh.7.7","rawR":"Neh.7.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.7","value":"Neh.7.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 7:7"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Azariah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Azariah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Azariah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Azariah #23"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Father of Ezra the scribe. Ezra returned to Jerusalem during the reign of King Artaxerxes I of Persia (464–424 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.1","r":"Ezra.7.1","rawR":"Ezra.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.1","value":"Ezra.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:1"},"). He is perhaps identical with #2 above, in which case Jehozadak would be Ezra’s brother."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. One of the priests who set his seal on the covenant of Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.2","r":"Neh.10.2","rawR":"Neh.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.2","value":"Neh.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Son of Hilkiah and a priest living in Jerusalem during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.11","r":"Neh.11.11","rawR":"Neh.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.11","value":"Neh.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:11"},"); called Azariah in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.11","r":"1Chr.9.11","rawR":"1Chr.9.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.11","value":"1Chr.9.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 9:11"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Azariah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Azariah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Azariah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Azariah #10"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the leaders of the priests who returned with Zerubbabel and Jeshua to Judah after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.1","r":"Neh.12.1","rawR":"Neh.12.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.1","value":"Neh.12.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:1"},"). His house in the next generation was headed by Meraiah. He is perhaps identical with #6 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Son of Azriel who, with Jerahmeel and Shelemiah, was ordered by King Jehoiakim of Judah (609–598 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") to capture Baruch and Jeremiah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.26","r":"Jer.36.26","rawR":"Jer.36.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.26","value":"Jer.36.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12. Son of Neriah and the official who accompanied King Zedekiah of Judah (597–586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") to Babylon. Seraiah was to relay Jeremiah’s message against Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.51.59-61","r":"Jer.51.59-61","rawR":"Jer.51.59-61","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.51.59-61","value":"Jer.51.59-61"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 51:59-61"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Seraiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","r